[EXPLAIN] How to read the summary tables
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Table 1: mean R2 over all outer folds for each molecular description, with its standard
  deviation (spread between         folds) and the number of folds. The top row is the best-
  performing description. Differences smaller than about one         standard deviation are
  usually not meaningful.
  Table 2: tests whether our R2 differs from the R2 values reported in the original publication
  (PAPER_R2). The         Nadeau-Bengio correction is applied because cross-validation folds
  overlap and share training data, which makes a         naive t-test over-confident.
  'Significant_p<0.05' = True means our result is really different from the reference
  (higher or lower: compare Our_R2_mean with Paper_R2); False means we reproduce it within
  statistical noise.
  The paired comparison at the end tests whether the two best descriptions differ from each other
  on the same folds.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

