~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] How to read the numbers below
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Mean difference in MAE (Morgan minus 2D/3D/FP) = +0.0063 pIC50 units. A negative value means
  Morgan makes smaller         errors on average. For scale: 0.3 pIC50 units is roughly a 2-fold
  change in potency (IC50).
  The t-statistic is the mean difference divided by its corrected uncertainty; |t| around 2 or
  more usually gives p < 0.05.         Only 25 folds are compared, so the test has limited power
  to detect small differences.
